  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W S Darley and obligated $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. W S Darley and won 2,176 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $551K, and obligations fell 19.3% year over year. W S Darley and received the vast majority of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.2B. W S Darley and obligations have grown since FY21, moving from $431M in FY21 to $1.5B in FY25 before recording $1.2B in FY26. W S Darley and sales are concentrated in two markets: Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $645M and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $510M. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations rather than full-year totals, so cumulative figures for FY2026 may change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers of W S Darley and this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.2B for W S Darley and in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $6.3M and the Department of Justice obligated $3.8M. Civilian agencies showed much smaller obligations, for example the Department of Homeland Security obligated $248K and the National Gallery of Art obligated $74K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and products account for most obligations?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market for W S Darley and at $645M. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing is the second-largest market at $510M. Smaller markets include Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing at $14M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $11.2M."
      }
    ]
